# EtSwipeableRow Component - Agent Guide

## Purpose & Scope

`EtSwipeableRow` is a list-row component that enables horizontal left-swipe to reveal action buttons. It uses a compound component pattern where content and actions are composed as sibling children.

**Location:** `/libs/etoro-ui/src/components/list/swipeable-row/`

**Key capabilities:**

- **Left-swipe gesture**: Pan gesture reveals action buttons positioned behind the content
- **Compound component pattern**: `EtSwipeableRow.Action` subcomponents define revealed buttons
- **Spring-based animation**: Snap-open / snap-closed with configurable spring physics
- **Uniform icon fade-in**: All action icons fade in together as the row is dragged open
- **Full-swipe shortcut (default ON)**: Drag past `fullSwipeThreshold` (default 60% of row width) and release to auto-trigger the LAST action — the last action's background expands across the row, a single medium haptic fires, then the last action's `onPress` runs (or `onFullSwipeCommit` if provided) and the row springs back to closed
- **Destructive opt-in (`collapseOnLastAction`)**: When set, BOTH a full-swipe commit AND a press of the LAST action animate the row's height to 0 before firing the callback (Telegram-style dismissal). Use for delete/archive rows.
- **List integration**: `isDragging` prop auto-closes swipe when parent list scrolls
- **Coordination callback**: `onSwipeStart` lets parents close other open rows (single-open-row pattern)

**Does NOT handle:**

- Right-to-left swipe (only left swipe is supported)
- Action state management (parent owns what actions exist and their handlers)
- Row selection or highlighting
- Sibling list-item reflow after a full-swipe commit (the row goes to height 0 before notifying the consumer; closing the gap in the surrounding list is the consumer's concern)

## Architecture

```text
EtSwipeableRow (Root)
├── SwipeableRowContext.Provider (shares closeSwipe, defaultButtonWidth)
├── View (container, overflow: hidden)
│   ├── View (actionsContainer, absolute right, contains Action elements)
│   │   └── EtSwipeableRow.Action × N (revealed on swipe)
│   └── GestureDetector → Animated.View (sliding content layer)
│       └── {contentChildren} (everything that is NOT an Action)
```

Children are automatically separated: `EtSwipeableRow.Action` elements go into the actions container; all other children become the sliding content layer.

## Component API

### `<EtSwipeableRow>`

Root container that wraps content and action buttons.

**Props (`EtSwipeableRowProps`):**

| Prop                    | Type                               | Required | Description                                                                                                       |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `children`              | `ReactNode`                        | Yes      | Content elements and `EtSwipeableRow.Action` subcomponents                                                        |
| `isDragging`            | `boolean`                          | No       | When `true`, auto-closes an open swipe. Wire to parent list drag state.                                           |
| `onSwipeStart`          | `(closeSwipe: () => void) => void` | No       | Called when a swipe begins on a closed row. Receives the row's `closeSwipe` function for single-open-row pattern. |
| `contentContainerStyle` | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>`             | No       | Style for the sliding content layer. Override `backgroundColor` when rendering on non-neutral surfaces.           |
| `enableFullSwipe`       | `boolean`                          | No       | Enables the Telegram-style "swipe all the way" shortcut for the LAST action. Default `true`.                      |
| `fullSwipeThreshold`    | `number`                           | No       | Fraction of row width past which a release commits the full-swipe. Range `(0, 1]`. Default `0.6`.                 |
| `onFullSwipeCommit`     | `() => void`                       | No       | Override called instead of the last action's `onPress` when a full-swipe commits.                                 |
| `collapseOnLastAction`  | `boolean`                          | No       | When `true`, both full-swipe commits AND presses of the LAST action animate the row's height to 0 before firing the callback. Default `false`. |

### `<EtSwipeableRow.Action>`

Action button revealed behind the content on left swipe. Must be a direct child of `EtSwipeableRow`.

**Props (`EtSwipeableActionProps`):**

| Prop                 | Type                   | Default | Description                                                 |
| -------------------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| `children`           | `ReactNode`            | -       | Content rendered inside the action (icon, text, etc.)       |
| `onPress`            | `() => void`           | -       | Called when tapped.                                         |
| `width`              | `number`               | `70`    | Width in pixels. Affects total snap distance.               |
| `style`              | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>` | -       | Container style. Use `backgroundColor` to color the action. |
| `testID`             | `string`               | -       | Stable automation identifier forwarded to the press target. |
| `accessibilityLabel` | `string`               | -       | Label for screen readers                                    |
| `accessibilityHint`  | `string`               | -       | Hint for screen readers                                     |
| `accessibilityRole`  | `AccessibilityRole`    | -       | Accessibility role                                          |
| `accessible`         | `boolean`              | -       | Whether the action is accessible                            |

## Usage Patterns

### Single action (delete)

```tsx
<EtSwipeableRow>
  <EtListItemV2 size="large">{/* row content */}</EtListItemV2>
  <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleDelete} style={{ backgroundColor: colors.statusNegative }}>
    <EtIconV2 name="trash" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
  </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
</EtSwipeableRow>
```

### Multiple actions

```tsx
<EtSwipeableRow onSwipeStart={handleSwipeStart}>
  <EtListItemV2 size="large">{/* row content */}</EtListItemV2>
  <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleTrade} style={{ backgroundColor: colors.bgNeutralSecondary }}>
    <EtIconV2 name="trade" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
  </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
  <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleDelete} style={{ backgroundColor: colors.statusNegative }}>
    <EtIconV2 name="trash" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
  </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
</EtSwipeableRow>
```

### Destructive row (`collapseOnLastAction`)

When the last action removes the row from the list (delete, archive, etc.), opt into the
height-collapse animation so the row visually disappears in lockstep with both a full-swipe
commit and a direct tap on the destructive action:

```tsx
<EtSwipeableRow collapseOnLastAction>
  <RowContent />
  <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleArchive} style={{ backgroundColor: colors.bgInfo }}>
    <EtIconV2 name="archive" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
  </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
  <EtSwipeableRow.Action
    onPress={() => removeFromList(item.id)}
    style={{ backgroundColor: colors.statusNegative }}
  >
    <EtIconV2 name="trash" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
  </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
</EtSwipeableRow>
```

The collapse fires the `onPress` callback only after the height animation completes — your
callback is responsible for removing the item from the underlying data so the surrounding
list closes the gap.

### Single-open-row pattern (in a list)

Only one row should be open at a time. Use `onSwipeStart` to close the previously open row:

```tsx
function SwipeableList({ items }) {
  const closeRef = useRef<(() => void) | null>(null);

  const handleSwipeStart = useCallback((closeSwipe: () => void) => {
    closeRef.current?.();
    closeRef.current = closeSwipe;
  }, []);

  return items.map((item) => (
    <EtSwipeableRow key={item.id} onSwipeStart={handleSwipeStart}>
      <RowContent item={item} />
      <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={() => handleDelete(item.id)} style={{ backgroundColor: colors.statusNegative }}>
        <EtIconV2 name="trash" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
      </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
    </EtSwipeableRow>
  ));
}
```

### Integration with list drag state

Close swipe when the parent list starts dragging (scrolling):

```tsx
const [isDragging, setIsDragging] = useState(false);

<FlashList
  onScrollBeginDrag={() => setIsDragging(true)}
  onScrollEndDrag={() => setIsDragging(false)}
  renderItem={({ item }) => (
    <EtSwipeableRow isDragging={isDragging}>
      <RowContent item={item} />
      <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={() => handleDelete(item.id)} style={{ backgroundColor: colors.statusNegative }}>
        <EtIconV2 name="trash" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
      </EtSwipeableRow.Action>
    </EtSwipeableRow>
  )}
/>;
```

### Custom action width

```tsx
<EtSwipeableRow.Action width={90} onPress={handleDelete} style={{ backgroundColor: colors.statusNegative }}>
  <EtIconV2 name="trash" size="lg" color={colors.textBright} />
</EtSwipeableRow.Action>
```

### Custom content background

When the row is rendered on a non-neutral surface, override the content background so it masks the actions correctly:

```tsx
<EtSwipeableRow contentContainerStyle={{ backgroundColor: colors.bgNeutralSecondary }}>{/* ... */}</EtSwipeableRow>
```

## Anti-patterns

### Using Action outside of EtSwipeableRow

```tsx
// BAD - throws: "EtSwipeableRow.Action must be used within an EtSwipeableRow component"
<EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleDelete}>
  <EtIconV2 name="trash" />
</EtSwipeableRow.Action>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap Actions inside an `EtSwipeableRow`.

### Wrapping Actions in intermediate components

```tsx
// BAD - child separation only checks direct children for SwipeableAction type
<EtSwipeableRow>
  <RowContent />
  <View>
    <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleDelete}>...</EtSwipeableRow.Action>
  </View>
</EtSwipeableRow>
```

**Fix:** Actions must be direct children of `EtSwipeableRow`. The `useSwipeableRowChildren` hook uses `Children.toArray` and checks `child.type === SwipeableAction` — wrapping in a `View` breaks type detection.

### Forgetting contentContainerStyle on colored backgrounds

```tsx
// BAD - default bgNeutralPrimary won't match a secondary surface
<View style={{ backgroundColor: colors.bgNeutralSecondary }}>
  <EtSwipeableRow>
    <RowContent />
    <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleDelete}>...</EtSwipeableRow.Action>
  </EtSwipeableRow>
</View>
```

**Fix:** Pass `contentContainerStyle={{ backgroundColor: colors.bgNeutralSecondary }}` to match the parent surface, otherwise the sliding layer creates a visible color mismatch.

### Not coordinating multiple swipeable rows

```tsx
// BAD - multiple rows can be open simultaneously
{
  items.map((item) => (
    <EtSwipeableRow key={item.id}>
      <RowContent />
      <EtSwipeableRow.Action onPress={handleDelete}>...</EtSwipeableRow.Action>
    </EtSwipeableRow>
  ));
}
```

**Fix:** Use the `onSwipeStart` callback with a `closeRef` to ensure only one row is open at a time (see "Single-open-row pattern" above).

## Swipe Animation Details

### Gesture configuration

- **Activation**: Horizontal pan activates at `±5px` offset (`activeOffsetX([-5, 5])`)
- **Conflict resolution**: Fails on vertical movement of `±10px` (`failOffsetY([-10, 10])`), yielding to vertical scrolling
- **Translation**: Clamped between `-totalSwipeWidth` and `0` (left swipe only)

### Snap logic

On gesture end, the row snaps open when **either**:

- Velocity exceeds `300` px/s in the swipe direction, **or**
- Translation exceeds 50% of `totalSwipeWidth`

Otherwise it snaps closed.

### Spring config

```text
damping: 50, stiffness: 300, overshootClamping: true
```

### Total swipe width

Calculated as the sum of all Action widths. Actions without an explicit `width` prop default to `70px`.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides `colors.bgNeutralPrimary` for default content background
- `SwipeableRowContext` - React Context sharing `closeSwipe` and `defaultButtonWidth` with Action subcomponents

### External Dependencies

- `react-native-gesture-handler` - `GestureDetector`, `Gesture.Pan()` for swipe gesture handling
- `react-native-reanimated` - `Animated.View`, `useAnimatedStyle`, `useSharedValue`, `withSpring` for animation
- `react-native-worklets` - `scheduleOnRN` to bridge worklet `onBegin` callback to JS thread for `onSwipeStart`
- `react-native` - `View`, `Pressable`, `StyleSheet`

