## Do's and Don'ts

### Do:

- Use `EtSwipeableRow.Action` as direct children of `EtSwipeableRow`
- Use `onSwipeStart` to implement single-open-row behavior in lists
- Use `isDragging` to close swipe when the parent list scrolls
- Set `contentContainerStyle` backgroundColor to match the parent surface
- Provide `accessibilityLabel` on each Action for screen reader support
- Use theme colors for action backgrounds (`colors.statusNegative` for destructive, etc.)

### Don't:

- Don't wrap Actions in intermediate View/Fragment containers (breaks child type detection)
- Don't use Actions outside of an EtSwipeableRow (will throw)
- Don't nest EtSwipeableRow components
- Don't set negative or zero `width` on Actions (falls back to default 70px)
- Don't forget to coordinate multiple rows in a list (use `onSwipeStart`)
- Don't rely on right-swipe — only left-swipe is supported
